{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1787","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. The Harmonization of XOR"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array of exactly $$$n$$$ numbers $$$[1,2,3,\\ldots,n]$$$ along with integers $$$k$$$ and $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Partition the array in exactly $$$k$$$ non-empty disjoint subsequences such that the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all numbers in each subsequence is $$$x$$$, and each number is in exactly one subsequence. Notice that there are no constraints on the length of each subsequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A sequence $$$a$$$ is a subsequence of a sequence $$$b$$$ if $$$a$$$ can be obtained from $$$b$$$ by the deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, for $$$n = 15$$$, $$$k = 6$$$, $$$x = 7$$$, the following scheme is valid: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[6,10,11]$$$, $$$6 \\oplus 10 \\oplus 11 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5,12,14]$$$, $$$5 \\oplus 12 \\oplus 14 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,9,13]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 9 \\oplus 13 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1,2,4]$$$, $$$1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 4 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[8,15]$$$, $$$8 \\oplus 15 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[7]$$$, $$$7 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" where $$$\\oplus$$$ represents the bitwise XOR operation."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following scheme is invalid, since $$$8$$$, $$$15$$$ do not appear: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[6,10,11]$$$, $$$6 \\oplus 10 \\oplus 11 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5,12,14]$$$, $$$5 \\oplus 12 \\oplus 14 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,9,13]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 9 \\oplus 13 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1,2,4]$$$, $$$1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 4 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[7]$$$, $$$7 = 7$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following scheme is invalid, since $$$3$$$ appears twice, and $$$1$$$, $$$2$$$ do not appear: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[6,10,11]$$$, $$$6 \\oplus 10 \\oplus 11 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5,12,14]$$$, $$$5 \\oplus 12 \\oplus 14 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,9,13]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 9 \\oplus 13 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,4]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 4 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[8,15]$$$, $$$8 \\oplus 15 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[7]$$$, $$$7 = 7$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and the only line of each test case contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$k$$$, $$$x$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$1\\le x \\le 10^9$$$) — the length of the array, the number of subsequences and the required XOR."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, if it is possible to partition the sequence, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in the first line. In the $$$i$$$-th of the following $$$k$$$ lines first print the length $$$s_i$$$ of the $$$i$$$-th subsequence, then print $$$s_i$$$ integers, representing the elements in the $$$i$$$-th subsequence. If there are multiple answers, print any. Note that you can print a subsequence in any order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is not possible to partition the sequence, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n15 6 7\n11 4 5\n5 3 2\n4 1 4\n6 1 7\n11 5 5\n11 6 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\n3 6 10 11\n3 5 12 14\n3 3 9 13\n3 1 2 4\n2 8 15\n1 7\nYES\n2 1 4\n2 2 7\n2 3 6\n5 5 8 9 10 11\nNO\nYES\n4 1 2 3 4\nYES\n6 1 2 3 4 5 6\nNO\nNO"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, we construct the following $$$6$$$ subsequences: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[6,10,11]$$$, $$$6 \\oplus 10 \\oplus 11 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5,12,14]$$$, $$$5 \\oplus 12 \\oplus 14 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,9,13]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 9 \\oplus 13 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1,2,4]$$$, $$$1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 4 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[8,15]$$$, $$$8 \\oplus 15 = 7$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[7]$$$, $$$7 = 7$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, we construct the following $$$4$$$ subsequences: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1,4]$$$, $$$1 \\oplus 4 = 5$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2,7]$$$, $$$2 \\oplus 7 = 5$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,6]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 6 = 5$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5,8,9,10,11]$$$, $$$5 \\oplus 8 \\oplus 9 \\oplus 10 \\oplus 11 = 5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following solution is considered correct in this test case as well: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[1,4]$$$, $$$1 \\oplus 4 = 5$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[2,7]$$$, $$$2 \\oplus 7 = 5$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[5]$$$, $$$5 = 5$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[3,6,8,9,10,11]$$$, $$$3 \\oplus 6 \\oplus 8 \\oplus 9 \\oplus 10 \\oplus 11 = 5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1787E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1787/problem/E"}